VERDICT for Option A v1 (smoke kernel: gradient-Hough on raw RGBA):

  S1 (radius floor)         REFUTED — XL42+ ratio range [0.38, 0.48] is a SUBSET of
                            Small [0.38, 0.45] and Mid [0.38, 0.57].  No threshold tau
                            separates the populations.

  S2 (concentration)        REFUTED — peakShare XL42+ median 0.17 vs Small 0.18, Mid 0.12.
                            Entropy XL42+ median 4.34 vs Small 4.35, Mid 4.52.  Overlap.

  Note: 11T has the HIGHEST ratio_med (0.68) of any cluster — the cropped FFT pipeline
  already correctly handles those (they go down the small-gear path).  But the diagnostic
  question is: "does the chainring (XL42+) regime present a distinguishable Hough signal?"
  Answer: not with this kernel.

Root cause hypothesis:
  - Raw downsampled RGBA contains: frame edges, hub/spindle features, BCD bolt circle,
    inner ramp lines, cogset behind chainring, hand/finger artifacts.  All cogwise
    concentric features.  Sobel + dense gradient Hough peaks on the strongest concentric
    feature, which on this corpus is almost always the BCD/hub circle at r~120-160px
    (regardless of true gear size).
  - To surface the OUTER ring specifically we'd need: (a) Canny pre-filter so only the
    clearest outer edge votes, (b) gradient-direction filter to suppress inner spider
    edges, OR (c) annular mask (aim-circle authoritative — Option B' territory again).

Recommendation:
  - DESCOPE v1 (smoke kernel) BEFORE calibration sweep — n=13 stratified diagnostic
    already shows S1/S2 inseparable, no value in n=145.
  - v2 candidates (escalation under PAP-1481, fresh subtask):
      v2a: Canny pre-filter + Hough Gradient (sparser, more selective edges).
      v2b: 3D accumulator (cx,cy,r) with proper argmax — confirms whether outer ring
           has a real peak hiding under inner-feature noise.
      v2c: Annular Hough — search only within aim-prior radius band [0.6, 1.4]*aimR
           (re-uses operator aim as authoritative annulus).
  - Comment on PAP-1489 with this verdict so QA does not spend cycles on v1 spec.
